// SYNTHESIZED (issue #789, lane R6): restart-survival check for side chat history. Used by
// scripts/verify-tauri-side-chat.mjs's second launch, which relaunches the built exe against the
// SAME `REFRACT_DATA_DIR` side-chat-live.jsonl's own run used (so the Session/repository registry
// persists across the relaunch, the one piece of real on-disk state this harness has). This fake
// `omp` process is a brand-new process with no memory of the earlier run, so it always answers
// `get_btw_history` with the topic that earlier run asked, regardless of what a real `omp` would
// have actually written to its own session file -- this proves ONLY that `sideChat.getHistory`
// reattaches, requests `get_btw_history`, and flattens the result correctly after a restart, not
// that OMP itself genuinely persisted the thread across the process boundary (no live `omp` ran
// in this harness to persist against; see README.md's own provenance table for every fixture's
// disclosed scope).
